{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The drawing, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, or nil when the graph has no planar embedding."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The drawing comes from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"planarEmbedding()"},{"text":" by de Fraysseix, Pach and Pollack’s shift method","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in Chrobak and Payne’s linear-time form. The embedding of the underlying simple graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(self-loops and parallel copies drawn as one segment) is first made connected, by an edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the first vertex of each component to the first vertex of the next, and every face","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"boundary a simple cycle; then every face but the largest (the outer face) is triangulated.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The vertices are placed in a canonical ordering of that graph, each one above the contour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of those before it, the contour shifted to make room. The added edges are not drawn and not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported. Every vertex has integer coordinates with 0 ≤ x ≤ 2n − 4 and 0 ≤ y ≤ n − 2, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two edges cross or overlap. Fewer than four vertices are placed at (0, 0), (2, 0) and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1, 1) in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order. The drawing is not rescaled (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rescaled(scale:center:)"},{"text":" maps it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to a common frame). A directed graph is drawn through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"undirectedView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"de Fraysseix, Pach and Pollack, “How to draw a planar graph on a grid”, Combinatorica"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10(1), 1990."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Chrobak and Payne, “A linear-time algorithm for drawing a planar graph on a grid”,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Information Processing Letters 54(4), 1995.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n + m) for the embedding, then O(n) expected (hashing the triangulation’s vertex pairs)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"As for ","type":"text"},{"code":"planarEmbedding()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition","type":"aside"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/planarlayout()"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarLayout()"},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"PlanarLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/PlanarLayout.swift#L31"},"title":"planarLayout()","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P0A7DrawingE12planarLayoutAD0C0Vy6VertexQzGSgyF","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A crossing-free straight-line drawing on an integer grid, or nil when the graph is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"planar."}],"references":{"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Graph","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/G